From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:46:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 106/111] ASoC: mediatek: add the MT8516 audio front end

From lidar-mainline by LeagueRaINi (GPL-2.0, commit db8242a), backported
to 6.12 for the MT8516 Echos (ADR 0031). lidar-mainline derived it from
the MediaTek/Amazon MT8167 driver in Amazon's 4.4 source release
(sound/soc/mediatek/mt8167/mt8167-afe-*.c).

What the Echos use: DL1 out to I2S (the speaker amplifier), 8-channel TDM
in (the microphone ADCs) and AWB, the loopback of what DL1 plays (the
echo reference). The internal codec's INT ADDA path is not here.
lidar-mainline's machine driver for the Echo Plus (2nd gen) is left out
until there is such a unit to test it on.
